# Sports Migration Standards

RULE: Sports pipeline services (features-sports-service, execution-service sports adapters, sports-strategy, sports-execution) MUST NOT import from sports-betting-services (footballbets). No PostgreSQL/psycopg2/SQLAlchemy in pipeline; data flows via GCS + PubSub only. No empty fallbacks; no dict[str, Any] at service boundaries. NOTE: unified-sports-execution-interface has been merged into execution-service.
WHY: Complete separation from legacy repo; Citadel-audit-worthy boundaries; fail-fast config.
CODEX: 04-architecture/sports-integration-plan.md (§ Phase 3), 06-coding-standards/integration-testing-layers.md

DO:
  Use UnifiedCloudConfig for all config; fail on missing keys
  Use Pydantic models from unified-api-contracts for every GCS write and PubSub message
  Run naming checks at Step A: rg 'from footballbets' . → 0; rg 'postgresql|psycopg2|sqlalchemy' . --type py → 0 in pipeline services
  Emit all 11 lifecycle events per service

NEVER:
  from footballbets (any module)
  os.getenv(KEY, '') or config.bucket or ""
  PostgreSQL/SQLAlchemy in features-sports-service, execution-service sports adapters, sports-strategy, sports-execution
  dict[str, Any] at GCS/PubSub boundaries

See: no-empty-fallbacks.mdc, batch-live-symmetry.mdc, event-logging.mdc.
